🛒 Olist E-Commerce Analytics Dashboard




📘 Project Overview

The Olist E-Commerce Analytics Dashboard provides a complete analysis of Brazil’s largest online marketplace — Olist — covering sales, customer behavior, logistics, and reviews.

This project integrates:

Python for data cleaning, feature engineering, and transformation,

MySQL for data storage and star schema modeling, and

Power BI for interactive visualization and reporting.

The dashboard enables stakeholders to monitor key KPIs, track revenue trends, optimize delivery operations, and analyze customer satisfaction metrics.

🧰 Tools & Technologies
Layer	Tools / Technologies
Data Preparation	Python (pandas, numpy, openpyxl, mysql.connector)
Data Storage & Modeling	MySQL (Star Schema Design)
Visualization & Reporting	Power BI Desktop, Power Query, DAX
Supporting Tools	Matplotlib, Excel, GitHub
🐍 Python Data Preparation

Libraries Used: pandas, numpy, mysql.connector, matplotlib, openpyxl

Process Summary

Data Loading & Cleaning

Imported 9 CSV datasets (orders, customers, products, sellers, geolocation, payments, reviews, etc.).

Removed duplicates, handled nulls, standardized column names.

Translated product categories from Portuguese → English.

Feature Engineering

Derived analytical fields:

delivery_days – time between purchase and delivery.

on_time – delivery performance indicator.

distance_km – calculated via Haversine formula.

freight_ratio – freight cost as % of revenue.

is_repeat_customer & days_since_last_order – retention metrics.

Segmented customers by spending percentile (High / Mid / Low Value).

Data Validation

Checked null values, data types, and outliers.

Ensured consistent data granularity (order_id + order_item_id).

Data Export

Exported clean dimension and fact tables for Power BI and MySQL:

dim_customers.csv

dim_sellers.csv

dim_products.csv

fact_orders.csv

🗄️ MySQL Database Design

Database: ecom_data
Schema Type: Star Schema (Fact + Dimension Tables)

Tables Created:

Fact_Orders – transaction-level orders, payments, deliveries, and reviews.

Dim_Customers – unique customer info with location.

Dim_Sellers – seller details and region mapping.

Dim_Products – product metadata and hierarchy.

Dim_Date – calendar table for time-based analytics.

Indexes and relationships were applied to ensure fast query performance and Power BI refresh efficiency.

📊 Dashboard Structure
Page	Description	Preview
Executive Summary	Consolidates KPIs: Total Revenue, Orders, Customers, Freight %, Repeat Rate, and YoY growth trends.	

Customer Insights	Segment analysis (High/Mid/Low Value), retention rate, and regional performance.	

Operations & Logistics	Delivery performance, cancellations, average delivery days, and freight analysis.	

Distance & Freight Analysis	Relationship between delivery distance, freight %, and operational efficiency.	

Reviews & Payments	Customer sentiment and payment method distribution.	

